<|channel>thought
<channel|>Fizzy Sparkwidget adjusted his oversized goggles as a tiger lunged from the jungle ferns. "Not today, you overgrown kitty!" he squeaked, waving his staff. Beside him, his Succubus, Lilith, let out a sultry laugh and lashed her whip, sending the beast stumbling back.

The humidity of Stranglethorn Vale was terrible for Fizzy’s complexion, but Lilith made the slog through the thick undergrowth bearable. As they moved toward a nearby raptor nest, Fizzy noticed a group of adventurers nearby. They were all accompanied by hulking, purple-skinned Voidwalkers. 

"Why do they all have those gloomy brutes?" Fizzy muttered, watching a Voidwalker tank a hit for a Mage. "Lilith is much more efficient."

Lilith just winked, her eyes glowing with mischief. She knew that while she was busy dancing and distracting, many players were actually seeing the "shadow" of her work elsewhere.

***

**Answer:** Because of the **Seduction** ability. When a Succubus uses Seduction, she becomes invisible/hidden to the target, making it appear as though the Warlock is questing alone or with no pet at all. [end of text]


